    "result_text": "All 64 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**. \n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and consolidated duplicate detection around it.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **New `Soundex` utility** (`util/Soundex.java`) \u2014 a standard American Soundex phonetic encoder used for the surname component of the identity key and for soft-match detection.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.identityKey`** \u2014 changed from the plain `telephone|email|householdId` string to a **full lower-case SHA-256 hex digest** (64 chars) over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`:**\n   - `requireUniqueIdentity` now rejects a create (409) when the **whole identity key** matches an existing non-deleted owner, instead of just comparing telephone. The email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `normalizeEmail`, before this check).\n   - Removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block entirely (`requireNoHouseholdDuplicate`, `sameEmail`, `normalizeEmailKey` and its call site), since duplicate detection is now the single identity key.\n   - `findPossibleDuplicate` (soft match) now triggers when **`soundex(lastName)` and postcode match but the identity key differs** \u2014 so two owners with the same surname and postcode but *different* telephones are created as a soft match (`possibleDuplicate=true`) rather than rejected.\n\n**Behavioural effect (per spec):** same lastName + postcode + different telephone \u2192 soft match instead of hard 409; a full identity repeat (same telephone/email/surname) still collides with 409; deleted owners are still ignored throughout.\n\n`householdId` itself is unchanged \u2014 it's still returned in the DTO and drives household-membership counting/level logic, which the tests (Cp11, Cp23, Cp36, Cp39, Cp51) continue to verify.",
